** ==========================================================================
** calculix_cantilever_c3d8.inp — CalculiX/Abaqus deck, Euler-Bernoulli check.
** A slender cantilever L=0.20, b=h=0.010 (SI: m), 10 C3D8 hexes along x, 1x1
** across the section. Root face x=0 fully built in (ENCASTRE). Tip face x=L
** loaded with a transverse force F=1000 N in -y (250 N / tip node).
**   Euler-Bernoulli tip deflection  delta = P L^3 / (3 E I),  I = b h^3 / 12
**     I = 0.010*0.010^3/12 = 8.3333e-10 ,  delta = 1000*0.2^3/(3*210e9*I)
**         = 1.5238e-5 m  (Timoshenko, shear-corrected, slightly larger).
** L/h = 20 (slender) so the incompatible-modes hex matches E-B to < 1 %.
** ==========================================================================
